Denote BC=x, then by the trapezoid-basis theorem, we can say that [[https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/AM-GM Inequality]] is applied here. So,\begin{align*}
20+8&>2\sqrt{5 \cdot 12}\\
28&>2\sqrt{60}\\
14&>\sqrt{60}
\end{align*}Expanding the square, we find that $x^2>196$, thus $x>14$. However, for a trapezoid we must have $x<\frac{5+20}{2}=12.5$. Thus the leftmost integral value is $\boxed{15}$.[/think] <answer>15</answer>

